    "body": "Closes #41140",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-07T11:06:24Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41188#discussion_r3725829076"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/41188"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3725829076"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "`frame_setheight` may silently clamp the height, so this can report success without actually growing the frame. Check `fr_height` after the call and fail on no op. This also makes `find_horizontally_resizable_frame` unnecessary here.\n\n\n```suggestion\n  int old_height = fr->fr_height;\n  frame_setheight(fr, old_height + 1, false);\n  if (fr->fr_height == old_height) {\n    emsg(_(e_noroom));\n    return false;\n  }\n```\n\n`resize_frame_for_status` has the same pattern and should probably be handled together. \n\ncc window expert @seandewar \n",
            "commit_id": "c559092398537e0ab0472056617280cfe7c2e37e",
            "created_at": "2026-08-06T04:09:49Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -7268,16 +7268,13 @@ static bool resize_frame_for_status(frame_T *fr)\n // @return Success or failure.\n static bool resize_frame_for_winbar(frame_T *fr)\n {\n-  win_T *wp = fr->fr_win;\n   frame_T *fp = find_horizontally_resizable_frame(fr);\n \n   if (fp == NULL || fp == fr) {\n     emsg(_(e_noroom));\n     return false;\n   }\n-  frame_new_height(fp, fp->fr_height - 1, false, false, false);\n-  win_new_height(wp, wp->w_height + 1);\n-  frame_fix_height(wp);\n+  frame_setheight(fr, fr->fr_height + 1, false);",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41188#discussion_r3725829076",
            "id": 3725829076,
            "line": null,
            "node_id": "PRRC_kwDOAPphoM7eE6PU",
